        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "recommendations",
            "multilineTextboxSpec": {
              "lines": [
                "## Strategic Recommendations for Freshmart Retail Performance\n",
                "\n",
                "### 📊 Key Performance Insights\n",
                "\n",
                "**Overall Performance (2025)**\n",
                "* **Total Revenue**: R17.7M across 64,330 transactions\n",
                "* **Average Basket**: R275.08 with 13.45 items per transaction\n",
                "* **Geographic Leaders**: Gauteng dominates with R8.4M (48% of revenue), followed by Western Cape (R5.8M) and KwaZulu-Natal (R3.4M)\n",
                "\n",
                "### 🏪 Store Format Optimization\n",
                "\n",
                "**Current Performance by Format:**\n",
                "* **Medium Format**: R276.69 avg basket (highest)\n",
                "* **Large Format**: R274.34 avg basket, 31,441 transactions (highest volume)\n",
                "* **Express Format**: R273.05 avg basket, 8,115 transactions\n",
                "\n",
                "**Recommendations:**\n",
                "1. **Expand Medium format stores** - They deliver the highest average basket value while maintaining good transaction volume (24,774)\n",
                "2. **Optimize Express stores** - While they have similar basket values, their lower transaction volume suggests potential for better site selection or marketing\n",
                "3. **Leverage Large format strength** - These drive the highest transaction volume; focus on maintaining traffic while working to increase basket size through cross-selling\n",
                "\n",
                "### 👥 Loyalty Program Enhancement\n",
                "\n",
                "**Current State:**\n",
                "* Non-members: R9.3M revenue (52.4%)\n",
                "* Loyalty members: R8.4M revenue (47.6%)\n",
                "\n",
                "**Critical Finding:** Despite similar numbers, loyalty members likely have higher frequency/lifetime value. Investigate:\n",
                "* Member vs non-member transaction frequency\n",
                "* Average basket comparison (not just total revenue)\n",
                "* Member retention and repeat purchase rates\n",
                "\n",
                "**Action Items:**\n",
                "1. **Aggressive enrollment campaign** - The nearly 50/50 split suggests untapped potential\n",
                "2. **Tiered rewards program** - Incentivize higher basket values for members\n",
                "3. **Personalized promotions** - Use purchase data to drive targeted offers\n",
                "\n",
                "### 🏢 Competitive Response Strategy\n",
                "\n",
                "**Stores Facing Competition:**\n",
                "* Multiple stores show \"Yes\" for nearby competitors (FreshMart Pretoria 3, Pretoria 6, etc.)\n",
                "* Avg basket values for stores with competitors: R266-271 vs R276-292 for non-competing stores\n",
                "\n",
                "**Immediate Actions:**\n",
                "1. **Price competitiveness audit** - Focus on stores with nearby competition\n",
                "2. **Service differentiation** - Enhance in-store experience and convenience\n",
                "3. **Localized promotions** - Target customers in competitive zones with special offers\n",
                "4. **Basket-building initiatives** - Cross-merchandising and bundling to increase transaction value\n",
                "\n",
                "### 📈 Seasonal & Trend Opportunities\n",
                "\n",
                "**Key Observations:**\n",
                "* **H1 performance** (R290 avg basket) outperforms H2 (R261 avg basket) by 11%\n",
                "* Transaction volume peaks in November-December (5,829 and 5,674 respectively)\n",
                "* February shows the lowest volume (4,840 transactions)\n",
                "\n",
                "**Recommendations:**\n",
                "1. **H2 promotion strategy** - Aggressive campaigns in Q3-Q4 to close the gap with H1\n",
                "2. **February revival campaign** - Address the post-holiday slump with targeted promotions\n",
                "3. **Inventory planning** - Align stock levels with seasonal patterns to minimize stockouts during peak periods\n",
                "\n",
                "### 💳 Payment Method Insights\n",
                "\n",
                "**Distribution:**\n",
